<section class="fasting-history-guide three-tool-knowledge" id="fasting-history-guide" aria-labelledby="fasting-history-guide-heading">
 <h2 id="fasting-history-guide-heading">Fasting tracker and Qada fasts: complete planning and evidence guide</h2>
 <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> A fasting tracker helps you <strong>organise days you have already decided to make up</strong>, record completed fasts and view the remaining number. It cannot determine how many Ramadan days you owe or whether Fidya or Kaffarah applies. <a href="https://quran.com/2/185" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Quran 2:185</a> refers to making up an equal number of other days for illness or travel, but personal exemptions and other circumstances require qualified interpretation.</p>
